<p>&#8220;Did you hear what Howells once said to a boring author who was trying to wring a compliment out of him? &#8216;I don&#8217;t know how it is,&#8217; said the author, &#8216;I don&#8217;t seem to <em>write</em> as well as I used to do.&#8217; &#8216;Oh, yes you do &#8212; indeed you do. You write as well as you ever did;&#8211; But your <em>taste</em> is improving.&#8221;</p>
<p>&#8212; From a <a href="https://archive.org/details/johnjaychapmanhi0000chap_d4s5/page/254/mode/2up">letter</a> from John Jay Chapman to Margaret Chanler, Nov. 30, 1911</p>
